1
00:00:01,020 --> 00:00:02,940
Senate Democrats leadership fight.

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,260
Will Van Hollen challenge Schumer?

3
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:10,233
Democrats just won control
of the United States Senate.

4
00:00:10,453 --> 00:00:12,795
And before the new Congress
even starts, a fight

5
00:00:12,795 --> 00:00:14,795
has broken out over who should lead them.

6
00:00:15,046 --> 00:00:17,124
Chuck Schumer, now the minority leader,

7
00:00:17,124 --> 00:00:19,575
would become majority
leader again in January,

8
00:00:19,575 --> 00:00:21,067
if his own caucus backs him.

9
00:00:21,287 --> 00:00:25,110
Senate Democrats are expected to vote
in December, by secret ballot,

10
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:26,797
and a simple majority decides.

11
00:00:27,018 --> 00:00:30,388
Schumer has led the party
in the Senate for about twelve years,

12
00:00:30,388 --> 00:00:33,491
and many Democrats say it
is time for generational change.

13
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,718
Enter Chris Van Hollen,
a progressive senator from Maryland.

14
00:00:37,938 --> 00:00:41,005
At first, he said he was not
looking to be the next leader,

15
00:00:41,005 --> 00:00:44,384
and that he was kicking the tires
on a run for president in 2028.

16
00:00:44,634 --> 00:00:48,377
He also declined to back Schumer,
saying the job should not be automatic.

17
00:00:48,597 --> 00:00:51,257
Then, on Monday, November
ninth, he reopened the door.

18
00:00:51,478 --> 00:00:55,005
He said he is in listening mode,
and that there should be no coronation.

19
00:00:55,225 --> 00:00:59,366
Reports say a draft effort is underway,
and that he is actively considering a run.

20
00:00:59,586 --> 00:01:02,884
Michigan Senator-elect Abdul
El-Sayed has already endorsed him.

21
00:01:03,1000 --> 00:01:07,187
Schumer says he expects to be
reelected as majority leader,

22
00:01:07,187 --> 00:01:09,889
and that he wants to focus
on what Americans want.

23
00:01:10,109 --> 00:01:12,648
Asked if he expected
a challenge, he answered, no.

24
00:01:12,898 --> 00:01:15,588
Senator Richard Blumenthal
still backs him, and Senator

25
00:01:15,588 --> 00:01:18,475
Kirsten Gillibrand praised him
for winning the Senate back.

26
00:01:18,695 --> 00:01:22,575
Reports describe him as the heavy
favorite, with no declared challenger.

27
00:01:22,795 --> 00:01:25,637
But a handful of Democrats
have declined to support him.

28
00:01:25,857 --> 00:01:29,649
Senator Elissa Slotkin of Michigan
has not ruled out her own ambitions,

29
00:01:29,649 --> 00:01:31,838
and says she will not back anyone without

30
00:01:31,838 --> 00:01:34,349
a concrete plan for the first
one hundred days.

31
00:01:34,570 --> 00:01:37,156
Critics on the right say
Schumer is losing his grip.

32
00:01:37,376 --> 00:01:40,882
Supporters of Van Hollen say the party
needs a bolder, fresher leader.

33
00:01:41,966 --> 00:01:43,354
So what happens next?

34
00:01:43,574 --> 00:01:47,779
The vote comes in December, and so far,
no challenger has officially declared.

35
00:01:48,029 --> 00:01:50,664
Van Hollen and Slotkin
are the names to watch.

36
00:01:50,884 --> 00:01:54,500
If Schumer holds on, he returns
as majority leader in January.

37
00:01:54,719 --> 00:01:56,577
If he does not, the party's new Senate

38
00:01:56,577 --> 00:01:59,020
majority could begin
with a very different leader.

39
00:02:00,433 --> 00:02:04,109
Time for a new leader, or stick
with Schumer? Tell me in the comments.
